{
  "preset_id": "linkedin_ctv",
  "platform": "LinkedIn",
  "display_name": "LinkedIn — Connected TV (CTV) Ads",
  "description": "Connected TV advertising. By far the strictest LinkedIn envelope: exact broadcast-style dimensions, a constant frame rate from a fixed set, and a high minimum bitrate.",
  "origin": "shipped",
  "ruleset_version": "2026-08-09.1",
  "last_verified_date": "2026-08-09",
  "byte_convention": "Decimal bytes (500 MB = 500,000,000).",
  "caveats": [
    "LinkedIn notes that CTV is currently in testing, and that meeting the recommended requirements does not guarantee delivery to all publishers.",
    "CTV requires a constant frame rate. PreflightQC fails a file only when variable frame rate is positively reported; when the container does not signal the mode, this is reported as unknown rather than guessed.",
    "The -23 LUFS integrated loudness target is a real published requirement, but measuring it needs a full decode-and-measure pass that exceeds what PreflightQC V1 does. It is reported as not measured, never as a pass or a failure.",
    "CTV creatives delivered as a third-party VAST tag are not files, so PreflightQC cannot inspect them."
  ],
